{
  "about": "M63.1: durable wakes. Each scenario starts from an empty agent_wakes and runs its steps in order, each at its own instant. admit offers matches as the renderer sends them (an event wake's key is 64 lowercase hex, its trigger 16, its agent process: and a handle of [a-z0-9-], its cause kind event) and answers how many were admitted, how many were already live, and each refusal in offer order. claim, finish and cancel name a wake by its key, meaning the latest wake admitted with it; claim answers started (the cause the run records and the subjects it took with it), deferred with its reasons, gone, or an error that writes nothing. finish ends the claimed run with a run outcome. pause pauses or resumes an agent on the fleet. expire cancels pending wakes past ttl_days. pending lists the pending wakes inside ttl_days, oldest first. rows lists every wake in admission order. Replayed by src-tauri/src/runtime/wakes.rs and src/lib/mockIpc.test.ts.",
  "ttl_days": 7,
  "coalesce_max": 20,
  "busy_retry_secs": 60,
  "budget_retry_secs": 600,
  "cancel_whys": ["paused", "trigger_changed", "agent_gone", "page_gone"],
